    "site_what_title": "TODO: What is MECP?",
    "site_what_p1": "TODO: When disaster strikes and cell towers go dark, volunteers and first responders rely on mesh radios to coordinate. But mesh radios carry very little data — often less than 200 bytes — and when teams speak different languages, critical meaning gets lost.",
    "site_what_p2": "TODO: MECP (Mesh Emergency Communication Protocol) solves this by encoding emergency situations into compact, structured messages. Each message starts with a severity level, followed by standardised codes from 12 categories — medical, terrain, weather, supplies, coordination, and more.",
